---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Services · Pravine Mani · AI, SEO, Marketing Automation & Agentic OS Consultancy" description="Four focus areas. Four engagement shapes. Fixed scope, fixed price. Built in code, shipped on Vercel.">


<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><span class="gr">$</span> cd ~/services <span class="you">→ what i build</span></div>
  <h1>Four engagement shapes.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Four focus areas: <a href="/services/ai/">AI</a>, <a href="/services/seo/">SEO + GEO</a>, <a href="/services/marketing-automation/">marketing automation</a>, <a href="/services/agentic-os/">Agentic OS</a>. Four engagement shapes: free scoping call, Audit, Sprint, Custom. Pricing brackets on every card. Written quote within 24 hrs of the call.</p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a href="/contact/" class="cta-btn">Book a 30-min call →</a>
    <a href="#builds" class="cta-btn secondary">See sample builds</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== PRIMARY ENGAGEMENTS ===== -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="label">engagement shapes</div>
    <h2>Four shapes. One operator.</h2>
    <p>Each shape is productized: fixed scope, fixed deliverables, written quote before signing. <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Scoping Call</strong> is the entry (free, 30 min). <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Audit</strong> when you don't know where AI fits yet (from $4,500). <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Sprint</strong> when the workflow fits in one sentence (from $4,500). <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Custom</strong> for anything multi-workflow (from $12K).</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 00 · SCOPING CALL -->
  <div class="tier-card reveal" id="scoping-call">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1"><span class="pulse"></span>00 · SCOPING CALL</div>
        <h3>A 30-minute call.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time">FREE · 30 MIN</div>
        <div class="slots">BY APPOINTMENT</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT IT IS</h4>
        <p>The starting point. We walk through one workflow, sharpen scope, decide which of the three paid shapes fits. Free.</p>
        <p>If none does, I'll say so on the call and send you to who or what's better.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT WE COVER</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>What's broken, or what should ship next</li>
          <li>Honest read on whether AI is the fix</li>
          <li>If yes: which shape matches</li>
          <li>Rough scope + cost in writing within 24 hrs</li>
          <li>If no: referral or alternative</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-foot">
      <span class="meta">FREE · REMOTE · 24-HR FOLLOW-UP</span>
      <a href="/contact/">→ BOOK CALL</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 01 · AUDIT -->
  <div class="tier-card featured reveal" id="audit">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1"><span class="pulse"></span>01 · AI SYSTEM AUDIT</div>
        <h3>Where AI returns the most hours.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time">FIXED-SCOPE WEEK · MOST POPULAR</div>
        <div class="slots">LIMITED CAPACITY</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT IT IS</h4>
        <p>A focused week. Three founder interviews, workflow audit, and a hunt for the 3-5 places AI, SEO, or automation returns measurable time.</p>
        <p>Output: a prioritized opportunity list, vendor recommendations, monthly cost projections, a 30-day build plan with milestones.</p>
        <p>Right fit if AI placement is unclear, or previous tools haven't stuck.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h4>DELIVERABLES</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>3× founder interviews · 60 min each</li>
          <li>Current-state workflow map</li>
          <li>Ranked opportunity list · effort × impact</li>
          <li>Vendor + cost projections per opportunity</li>
          <li>30-day execution plan with milestones</li>
          <li>60-min handoff call + Loom walkthrough</li>
          <li>Option to roll into a build sprint</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-foot">
      <span class="meta">FROM $4,500 · REMOTE · LIMITED</span>
      <a href="/contact/">→ BOOK AUDIT CALL</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 02 · SPRINT -->
  <div class="tier-card reveal" id="sprint">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1" style="color: var(--red);"><span class="pulse" style="background: var(--red);"></span>02 · BUILD SPRINT</div>
        <h3>One workflow, shipped in a fixed window.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time" style="color: var(--red);">FIXED-SCOPE BUILD</div>
        <div class="slots">LIMITED CAPACITY</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT IT IS</h4>
        <p>Productized scope, fixed timeline. Monday morning we agree on one workflow. Wednesday EOD it's deployed and documented.</p>
        <p>The workflow has to be one-line specific. "Send this draft to my inbox at 6am." If it isn't, the sprint doesn't fit. The 3-day clock forces clarity on both sides.</p>
        <p><strong>Common scopes:</strong> daily morning brief. Weekly metrics report. Sales follow-up automation. Content cross-poster. AI-graded inbox triage.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h4>DELIVERABLES</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>One workflow · clear input + output</li>
          <li>Deployed on your Vercel (or mine)</li>
          <li>README · cost projection · env-var spec</li>
          <li>15-min handoff Loom + architecture diagram</li>
          <li>14 days of post-sprint bug fixes</li>
          <li>You own the code outright</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-foot">
      <span class="meta">FROM $4,500 · 50% UPFRONT · LIMITED</span>
      <a href="/contact/">→ BOOK SPRINT CALL</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 03 · CUSTOM -->
  <div class="tier-card reveal" id="custom">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1" style="color: var(--blue);"><span class="pulse" style="background: var(--blue);"></span>03 · CUSTOM BUILD</div>
        <h3>Bigger than a sprint. More specific than an agency.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time" style="color: var(--blue);">QUOTE-BASED</div>
        <div class="slots">LIMITED CAPACITY</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT IT IS</h4>
        <p>For multi-workflow builds that need more than a sprint. Free scoping call, written spec + quote within 24 hrs. Milestone-paid. Daily updates. Demo each milestone.</p>
        <p><strong>Reference shipped:</strong> CISNET marketing site rebuild (Next.js 16 + 200+ pSEO pages + Facebook Lead Ads pipeline + custom admin portal). Q4 2025. Three months solo.</p>
        <p>If a scope doesn't fit a productized box, it lives here.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h4>DELIVERABLES</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>30-min scoping call (free)</li>
          <li>Written spec within 24 hrs</li>
          <li>Milestone-based delivery</li>
          <li>Your stack OR my recommended stack</li>
          <li>Daily progress updates</li>
          <li>Architecture diagram + cost projections</li>
          <li>Full source + deployment instructions</li>
          <li>30 days of post-launch fixes</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-foot">
      <span class="meta">FROM $12K · MILESTONE-PAID</span>
      <a href="/contact/">→ START SCOPING</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== WHO THIS WORKS FOR (positive filter) ===== -->
<section class="section" id="for">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="label">who this works for</div>
    <h2>The shape of buyer this fits.</h2>
    <p>Three concrete subtypes. If you recognize yourself here, the engagement is built for you.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="for-grid">
    <div class="for-card reveal">
      <div class="check">✓</div>
      <h4>Bootstrapped SaaS founders</h4>
      <p>$200K-$3M ARR, 1-8 people. Already technical. Need workflows shipped: onboarding sequences, billing webhooks, AI-augmented features, internal ops automation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="for-card reveal">
      <div class="check">✓</div>
      <h4>Marketing / creative / content agencies</h4>
      <p>5-20 people, founder-led, $1-5M revenue. Need internal tooling, creative-variants generators, lead pipelines for clients, white-label dashboards, content engines.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="for-card reveal">
      <div class="check">✓</div>
      <h4>Tech-forward SMBs and consultancies</h4>
      <p>Small teams with technical leadership. No procurement cycles. Marketing sites, lead infrastructure, admin portals, programmatic SEO surfaces. The CISNET pattern.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== WHO I'M NOT FOR (filter block) ===== -->
<section class="section" id="not-for">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="label" style="color: var(--red);">honest filter</div>
    <h2>Who I'm <em>not</em> for.</h2>
    <p>Saves us both a call. If any of these describe you, the engagement won't work.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="not-for-grid">
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>Enterprises with procurement cycles</h4>
      <p>Vendor MSA. 6-week security review. SOC 2 audit before signing. I'm one person. That overhead breaks the economics. Hire an agency.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>n8n / Make / Zapier rebuilds only</h4>
      <p>If you want a no-code workflow strung together in a visual editor, I'm the wrong consultant. I work in code. If your existing stack is correct, I'll say so and refund.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>Sub-$2K projects</h4>
      <p>Below mid four-figures, scoping overhead is bigger than the work. Hire a freelance dev for one-off tasks at that size.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>Hourly billing engagements</h4>
      <p>Every engagement is fixed-scope, fixed-price. Hourly aligns nobody's incentives. If you need T&amp;M billing, we won't work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>AI-safety / AGI / RLHF research</h4>
      <p>Not my lane. Hire someone closer to the frontier labs. I build ops workflows, not alignment models.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="not-for-card reveal">
      <div class="x">✗</div>
      <h4>Customer-service chatbot work</h4>
      <p>Saturated category. Intercom Fin, Forethought, Ada are better at it than I'll ever be. I'll send you to them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

</section>

<!-- ===== SPECIFIC BUILDS GRID ===== -->
<section class="section" id="builds">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="label">sample builds</div>
    <h2>Eleven things I've shipped.</h2>
    <p>Real workflows. Each ships as a 3-day Sprint or gets customized to your stack. If a build isn't here, it lives in Custom.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="builds-grid">

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">$</div><span class="num">BUILD 01</span></div>
      <h4>Content Engine</h4>
      <p>One source article → 6+ platform variants. X thread, LinkedIn carousel, newsletter, video script, Reddit, podcast intro. RSS-triggered. AI-drafted. You approve before ship.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>~$0.04/run</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">▸</div><span class="num">BUILD 02</span></div>
      <h4>Customer Onboarding Sequence</h4>
      <p>Whop webhook (or Stripe / Lemon Squeezy) → Claude personalizes welcome → tags subscriber → triggers Day-0 to Day-30 sequence. Wired on the AOF stack.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>~$0.012/signup</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">▣</div><span class="num">BUILD 03</span></div>
      <h4>Daily Operations Brief</h4>
      <p>06:00 ET summary in your inbox. Stalled deals. Urgent items. Today's priorities. Metrics movement. Pulls from CRM + calendar + email. AI flags what matters.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>~$0.08/day</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">◐</div><span class="num">BUILD 04</span></div>
      <h4>Competitor Watch + Weekly Intel</h4>
      <p>Scans 6+ competitors across pricing pages, launch blogs, X, changelogs. Flags pricing changes and launches. Weekly intel report drafted Sunday night. Lands in your inbox Monday morning.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>~$0.12/day</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">⌘</div><span class="num">BUILD 05</span></div>
      <h4>Claude Code Stack Setup</h4>
      <p>Install and configure Claude Code for your whole team. Custom CLAUDE.md, sub-agents, hooks, MCP servers tuned to your stack. Training + cheatsheet included.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>1-DAY ENGAGEMENT</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">⊞</div><span class="num">BUILD 06</span></div>
      <h4>Design System Application</h4>
      <p>Apply a unified design language to your existing app. Token system. Component patterns. Voice rules. Audit + migration plan included. Built on Terminal DS or your brand.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>1–2 WEEKS</span><span class="ev">CUSTOM</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">◊</div><span class="num">BUILD 07</span></div>
      <h4>Community Platform Build</h4>
      <p>Full community workspace. Whop, Skool, or custom on your stack. Member auth. Gated content. Weekly drop cadence. AI coach. Automated onboarding. Reference: AIOpsForge.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>3–4 WEEKS</span><span class="ev">CUSTOM</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">⌖</div><span class="num">BUILD 08</span></div>
      <h4>SEO + GEO Infrastructure</h4>
      <p>Schema markup. JSON-LD. Per-page OG images. Sitemap. Robots. FAQ schema. llms.txt for AI-search engines. Built to rank in Google, Perplexity, and ChatGPT search.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>3–5 DAYS</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">∞</div><span class="num">BUILD 09</span></div>
      <h4>Lead-Magnet → CRM Pipeline</h4>
      <p>Landing page + gated PDF → Beehiiv, Kit, or ConvertKit → tagged + sequenced. AI personalizes follow-ups. Stripe or Whop checkout wired in. Plausible analytics + funnel tracking.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>3–5 DAYS</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">⚙</div><span class="num">BUILD 10</span></div>
      <h4>MCP Server (Custom)</h4>
      <p>Custom Model Context Protocol server. Connects Claude to your internal tools, data, or APIs as first-class actions. Examples: Notion-MCP, Linear-MCP, your-CRM-MCP.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>2–4 DAYS</span><span class="ev">CUSTOM</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="build-card reveal">
      <div class="icon-row"><div class="icon">▤</div><span class="num">BUILD 11</span></div>
      <h4>Creative Variants Generator</h4>
      <p>One brief → N image and copy variants for an ad set. Brand-tone guardrails baked in. Approve, reject, regenerate. Built for agencies running paid creative at volume.</p>
      <div class="meta"><span>~$0.05/variant</span><span class="ev">SPRINT-READY</span></div>
    </div>

  </div>

</section>

<!-- ===== FAQ ===== -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="label">questions</div>
    <h2>Questions I actually get.</h2>
    <p>If yours isn't here, ask on the call.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-block">
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>What do prices actually look like?</summary><p>Brackets are on the cards above. <span class="acc">Audit + Sprint from $4,500. Custom from $12K.</span> The final number depends on scope and your stack. Lands in writing within 24 hrs of the call.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>What stack do you build on?</summary><p><span class="acc">Claude Code. Vercel (serverless, cron, KV). Anthropic API.</span> I'll work in yours if it matches: TypeScript, Next.js, Supabase, Stripe, Beehiiv, Whop. I <strong>won't</strong> build on n8n, Make, or Zapier. Fragile, expensive at scale, unreadable six months later.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Who owns the code?</summary><p><span class="acc">You. Outright.</span> Work-for-hire under a written agreement. Full source, the deployment, the right to modify or sell. I retain nothing.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Why fixed price instead of hourly?</summary><p>Hourly aligns incentives badly. I'd be incentivized to drag. You'd be incentivized to micro-manage. Fixed-price aligns both sides on outcome.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>What if I'm in a different timezone?</summary><p>I'm in Toronto (ET). Async-default: Slack or email + recorded Loom updates. Live calls in your timezone between 9am and 9pm ET. Outside that, written-first.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>What if the scope changes mid-project?</summary><p>For sprints: scope is fixed, period. For audits + custom builds: anything outside the written spec is a separate quote. Never silently re-scope.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>Can you start next week?</summary><p>Usually yes for sprints. Sometimes for custom builds. Audits book 2-3 weeks out.</p></details>
    <details class="faq-item"><summary>What if I'm not sure I need an AI engagement at all?</summary><p>Book the call anyway. If AI isn't the right fix, I'll say so and send you to who or what is.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>




</Base>
<style is:global>
/* Reveal-on-scroll */
.reveal { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); transition: all 600ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1); }
.reveal.visible { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }

/* Sticky call-to-action band */
.cta-band { background: var(--bg-card); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 24px 28px; margin: 32px 0; }
.cta-band-inner { max-width: 1440px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 clamp(20px, 2.5vw, 48px); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; }
@media (min-width: 2000px) { .cta-band-inner { max-width: 1760px; } } @media (min-width: 3000px) { .cta-band-inner { max-width: 2200px; } } @media (min-width: 4400px) { .cta-band-inner { max-width: 2800px; } }
.cta-band .left { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
.cta-band .lab { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--green); text-transform: uppercase; }
.cta-band .h { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); }
.cta-band .h .acc { color: var(--green); }

/* Featured tier (audit/sprint/advisory/custom) */
.tier-card { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); margin-bottom: 22px; position: relative; transition: all 400ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1); }
.tier-card::before { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 2px; background: var(--card-accent, var(--green)); opacity: 0.85; }
.tier-card:hover { border-color: var(--border-green); transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4); }
.tier-card.featured { border-color: var(--border-green); }
.tier-head { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 20px; padding: 24px 30px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--bg-tertiary); align-items: center; }
.tier-head .left .row1 { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--green); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
.tier-head .left .row1 .pulse { width: 6px; height: 6px; background: var(--green); animation: pulse-dot 1.6s infinite; }
.tier-head .left h3 { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: clamp(22px, 1.9vw, 32px); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.15; }
.tier-head .right { text-align: right; }
.tier-head .right .time { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; color: var(--green); letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 2px; }
.tier-head .right .slots { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 9px; color: var(--text-dim); letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.tier-body { padding: 26px 30px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; gap: 32px; }
.tier-body .col h4 { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--green); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 12px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.tier-body .col p { font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif; font-size: clamp(14.5px, 1.05vw, 17.5px); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 12px; }
.tier-body .col p strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
.tier-body .col ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
.tier-body .col ul li { padding-left: 18px; position: relative; font-size: clamp(13.5px, 1vw, 16.5px); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.55; }
.tier-body .col ul li::before { content: '+'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--green); font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-weight: 600; }
.tier-foot { padding: 16px 30px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--bg-tertiary); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.tier-foot .meta { color: var(--text-dim); }
.tier-foot a { color: var(--bg-primary); background: var(--green); padding: 8px 14px; transition: all var(--dur-micro, 150ms) var(--ease); }
.tier-foot a:hover { background: var(--text-primary); }
.tier-foot a.secondary { background: transparent; color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
.tier-foot a.secondary:hover { background: var(--green); color: var(--bg-primary); }

.tier-card:nth-of-type(1) { --card-accent: var(--text-dim); }
.tier-card:nth-of-type(2) { --card-accent: var(--green); }
.tier-card:nth-of-type(3) { --card-accent: var(--red); }
.tier-card:nth-of-type(4) { --card-accent: var(--blue); }

/* Canadian grant callout */
.grant-callout { max-width: 1440px; margin: 0 auto 28px; padding: 0 clamp(20px, 2.5vw, 48px); }
